{:edb/db-before-t 447 :edb/db-after-t 448 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533760 50 #inst "2026-10-04T20:09:39.205Z" 13194139533760 true] [17592186124591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249821 13194139533760 true] [17592186124592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249804 13194139533760 true] [17592186124592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249807 13194139533760 true] [17592186124592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249814 13194139533760 true] [17592186125117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533760 true] [17592186125117 1145 "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249804 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249805 13194139533760 true] [17592186249804 1089 "q-344144" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249804 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533760 true] [17592186249804 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)-\\sqrt{3}}{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249804 1113 #uuid "53d8dce8-397e-5b28-942d-ca10c6ec8958" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249804 1145 "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)-\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}-\\sqrt{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{0}{1}-\\sqrt{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249806 13194139533760 true] [17592186249805 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533760 true] [17592186249805 1041 "field-1" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249805 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249806 13194139533760 true] [17592186249805 1110 #uuid "f63c5db5-f691-540b-9e7a-8e469bf7467b" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249806 1034 "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249806 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249806 1111 #uuid "87355fde-3a83-5901-b6ea-80f76125edb8" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249807 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249808 13194139533760 true] [17592186249807 1089 "q-37290" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249807 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533760 true] [17592186249807 1100 "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /3)}({tan}^{2}⁡(x)+3{cot}^{2}⁡(x)).$" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249807 1113 #uuid "f66a0076-8574-55ea-a46f-4caf92c84b78" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249807 1145 "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /3)}({tan}^{2}⁡(x)+3{cot}^{2}⁡(x)) & ={tan}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+3{cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}))}^{2}+3{(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =3+3(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =3+1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249809 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249810 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249811 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249812 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249813 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1041 "selection" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249812 13194139533760 true] [17592186249808 1110 #uuid "096cbec5-fcc3-593e-afc5-bfeeb320293a" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249809 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249809 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249809 1111 #uuid "90b0c1db-1464-5b9d-bad0-871611c51628" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249810 1034 "2" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249810 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249810 1111 #uuid "f97217f2-5e66-58e4-910c-fbbb053d88c0" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249811 1034 "6" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249811 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249811 1111 #uuid "bafa0292-1d6c-5d62-9fd2-2b50a61d6b9e" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249812 1034 "4" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249812 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249812 1111 #uuid "31a45a7a-e3a3-5027-9f45-c40d6a03ce41" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249813 1034 "\\frac{10}{3}" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249813 1111 #uuid "2cb905d6-ee04-50d8-ae0e-e6e556d3157c" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249814 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249815 13194139533760 true] [17592186249814 1089 "q-47039" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249814 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533760 true] [17592186249814 1100 "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249814 1113 #uuid "f27fcbd4-06f3-5af1-bede-4104ac6aed00" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249814 1145 "First, let's attempt to evaluate the limit by direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x) & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined.\n\nTherefore, to find the limit, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940317/assets/5e9d0e9d944cda9c97555ffdeac5aa245905f800cd99e11f5d172203bad3892d.png)\n\nAs $x$ approaches $\\pi $ from the left, the values of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)$ are negative and decrease without bound. Therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)=-\\infty \n$$\n\nHowever, as $x$ approaches $\\pi $ from the right, the values of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)$ are positive and grow without bound. Therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{+}}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)=\\infty \n$$\n\nSince the two limits are not equal, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249816 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249817 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249818 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249819 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249820 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1041 "selection" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249819 13194139533760 true] [17592186249815 1110 #uuid "858e1d30-0d11-5afe-a048-c186050fe839" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249816 1034 "\\infty " 13194139533760 true] [17592186249816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249816 1111 #uuid "7a1f60af-0def-5ccf-b6e5-9b9a73c575fd" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249817 1034 "-\\infty " 13194139533760 true] [17592186249817 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249817 1111 #uuid "ad57914d-3578-5cc1-839e-47970a85f5af" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249818 1034 "1" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249818 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249818 1111 #uuid "4f493888-cc2b-5ce9-aa9f-04a97d836676" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249819 1034 "\\text{DNE}" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249819 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249819 1111 #uuid "af1fac2c-3620-5983-b1bf-b23907d5f8e5" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249820 1034 "0" 13194139533760 true] [17592186249820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533760 true] [17592186249820 1111 #uuid "118c35c4-01b9-518d-b489-1e1bd00c5418" 13194139533760 t